{
  "_doc": "Markets, tradable goods, and FX exchange config (E1 — simulated, no server). A `market` is a venue (a Scene's marketplace or a global exchange) quoting goods in its `localCurrency`. A `good` reuses an existing trade-good item id (content/items/catalog.json) and gives it a market mid-price (in the local currency's MINOR units) + a per-good volatility/spread. `priceSim` walks each good's mid deterministically (seeded by day+id) so solo play has a living, reproducible market. `exchange` config holds the NPC money-changer default spread (bps). CDN-overridable.",
